# Living Survey: brain                                                                                               
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Introduction                                                                                                      
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
This document collects the scientific literature regarding **brain**.                                                
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Brain Tumor Diagnostics and Segmentation                                                                          
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
Recent advances in medical imaging and AI have significantly improved the detection and segmentation of brain tumors.
NeuroTS-Net introduces a three-dimensional encoder-decoder architecture that preserves fine intensity and boundary   
information for pediatric brain tumor segmentation, outperforming baseline methods on the BraTS 2026 dataset         
[^2609.16873]. Similarly, DE-GAN employs a contrast-enhancing conditional GAN to synthesize slice-adaptive FLAIR     
images, improving segmentation of enhancing tumors and tumor cores across multiple BraTS datasets [^2609.16755]. For 
comprehensive diagnosis, BrainVLM integrates MRI scans, demographics, and radiology reports to classify all 12 WHO   
2021 brain tumor types, providing diagnostic uncertainty quantification and report generation [^2609.16597]. The     
generalization of conventional models like nnU-Net across heterogeneous populations has also been evaluated,         
revealing challenges with small or disconnected tumor components [^2609.15524]. Furthermore, machine unlearning      
techniques like GRIN+ address privacy regulations in imbalanced medical data, maintaining diagnostic accuracy while  
erasing sensitive patient records [^2609.15571].                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
Beyond imaging, liquid biopsy and epigenetic profiling offer non-invasive diagnostic avenues. Analyses of cell-free  
DNA (cfDNA) reveal nucleosome positioning signatures in glioblastoma multiforme (GBM), providing potential biomarkers
for early detection [^10.5526_err-00042862][^10.5526_err-00042900]. Single-cell spatially resolved atlases of        
pan-cancer metastatic brain tumors are being developed to map the tumor microenvironment at unprecedented resolution 
[^10.5281_zenodo.21782884][^10.5281_zenodo.21782885][^10.5281_zenodo.21816284][^10.5281_zenodo.21816285]. Therapeutic
strategies are also evolving, with lipid nanoparticle-mediated siRNA delivery targeting TERT showing robust gene     
silencing and cytotoxic effects in GBM cell lines [^10.17030_uclan.thesis.00059253][^10.17030_uclan.thesis.00059033].
Additionally, secretomes and extracellular vesicles from neural crest-derived stem cells have demonstrated the       
ability to inhibit GBM proliferation and modulate immune responses [^10.48683_1926.00128572].                        
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Neural Decoding and EEG Analysis                                                                                  
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
Electroencephalography (EEG) and brain signal analysis continue to benefit from large-scale benchmarks and foundation
models. iMINDBench establishes a standardized framework for iEEG neural decoding across multiple institutions and    
naturalistic tasks, highlighting the need for models that generalize across subjects and preprocessing pipelines     
[^2609.18104]. For broader brain signal analysis, METIS introduces a language-guided multimodal foundation model     
pretrained on over 70,000 hours of recordings, achieving state-of-the-art zero-shot and few-shot performance across  
12 datasets without fine-tuning [^2609.15740]. In psychiatric applications, CNN-Transformer hybrids for schizophrenia
detection from EEG spectrograms achieve high classification accuracy while ensuring subject-level data partitioning  
to prevent leakage [^2609.14015].                                                                                    
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
Advancements in generative decoding also show promise, with Mind2Cloud proposing a two-granularity diffusion         
framework to reconstruct 3D point clouds from EEG signals, dynamically adapting spatial granularity to match the     
coarse-to-fine denoising trajectory [^2609.13991]. Furthermore, nonparametric correlation estimators are being       
applied to analyze dynamic functional connectivity across six frequency bands, offering new insights into neural     
interactions [^2609.13848]. In developmental neuroscience, EEG microstates are being linked to infant temperament    
attributes, providing a window into early self-regulation and emotional reactivity [^10.7273_000007929].             
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Computational Neuroscience and Digital Twins                                                                      
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
Theoretical and computational models are increasingly bridging biological realism with hardware efficiency. Scaled   
hippocampus-inspired spiking neural networks are being mapped to neuromorphic memristive hardware, demonstrating     
biologically realistic resting-state dynamics and energy efficiency [^2609.16429]. At the systems level, brain-based 
digital twins (BB-DTs) are being formalized to integrate EEG with kinematic data for real-time motor imagery         
feedback, validated through synthetic data augmentation and closed-loop coaching interfaces                          
[^10.17870_bathspa.00017805]. A new stochastic model combining Random Neural Networks and Markov-Modulated Poisson   
Processes aims to improve the fidelity of whole-brain digital twins by capturing mechanisms across multiple scales   
[^2609.13973].                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
Neuroevolutionary studies also challenge traditional hypotheses, showing that larger neural networks in dynamic      
environments often arise from prior static evolution rather than direct adaptation to changing conditions            
[^2609.15569]. On the molecular level, circular RNAs (circRNAs) are identified as stable biomarkers of biological    
aging in the brain, accumulating at rates corresponding to physiological rather than chronological age               
[^10.48617_etd.1568]. Additionally, moderate neural noise has been shown to be critical for accurate internal        
simulation of rare events in Bayesian neural networks, compensating for sampling errors and offering a framework for 
understanding disorders like Parkinson's [^2609.18033]. Graphlet-based structural fingerprints are also proving      
effective for capturing local-to-mesoscopic topology in complex networks, including resting-state functional         
connectomes [^2609.17445].                                                                                           
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Neurodegeneration, Metabolism, and Sensory Systems                                                                
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
Longitudinal disease progression modeling is being revolutionized by reverse spatio-temporal approaches. By using    
Neural Ordinary Differential Equations in a discrete latent space, models can now reconstruct unobserved healthier   
brain anatomy from later diseased states, aiding early intervention strategies for Alzheimer's disease [^2609.14590].
The amyloid precursor protein (APP) is also being re-evaluated not merely as a pathological substrate but as a       
universal survival molecule, raising critical questions about broad-spectrum APP suppression therapies               
[^10.5281_zenodo.20049820].                                                                                          
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
Metabolic profiling of human arteriovenous blood samples has revealed extensive cross-organ metabolite exchange,     
identifying 245 significant instances of organ-specific uptake and release, including brain-specific patterns        
[^10.5281_zenodo.20652505][^10.5281_zenodo.20652506]. In Parkinson's disease, aerobic exercise is proposed to reshape
nitric oxide signaling toward adaptive profiles that may enhance mitophagy and neuroprotection                       
[^10.4103_mgr.medgasres-d-26-00008].                                                                                 
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
Sensory and developmental neurobiology continues to uncover intricate mapping mechanisms. A spatial code governing   
olfactory receptor choice aligns sensory maps in both the nose and brain through a dorsoventral gradient in retinoic 
acid signaling [^10.5281_zenodo.18941307][^10.5281_zenodo.18941308]. In the hindbrain, cholecystokinin (CCK)         
signaling in the nucleus of the solitary tract is blunted by high-fat diets, linking central vagal afferents to      
satiety and obesity pathways [^10.7273_000008411]. Finally, gray matter volumes in semantic control regions are shown
to interact with age and culture, influencing cognitive categorization and retrieval strategies [^10.48617_etd.1671].
                                                                                                                     

